      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Shame to see that this suggestion has been sitting here for so long, but I'd really like to this this (there was a mod that did this before called InstanceDejavu).\nSometimes when you are hopping around, you might go into an intance that you don't really like and want to avoid, so you hop over to an alternative instance of that world. It's really hard to know which instances you've already visited previously, so you end up accidentally rejoining the instances you were trying to avoid!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-12T18:24:34.297Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Could something be added to show which instances of a world that you have visited? I joined a lot of public worlds and it gets very tedious checking the instance ID to see if I had visited it already.",
